## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to build a practical autocomplete index with dynamic updates, using common data structures and real-world trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-word counts
- Dynamic frequency updates via a hashmap
- Top-k selection with a bounded DFS and a small heap
- Trade-offs: update cost vs lookup speed; memory use for prefixes

## Code Example
```javascript
class Autocomplete {
  constructor() {
    this.root = {};
    this.words = new Map();
  }
  addWord(word, delta) {
    this.words.set(word, (this.words.get(word) || 0) + delta);
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of word) {
      node = node[ch] = node[ch] || {};
    }
    node.__end = word;
  }
